// The unknown-condition rule is checked every time the condition is evaluated,
// not only on the way in. `u || i < 2` is true for two iterations (unknown OR
// true is true) and unknown on the third (unknown OR false is unknown), so the
// loop must run twice and then be refused. A check made only before the first
// iteration would let it run on; reading unknown as false would let it finish.
u: bool = ?
i: t64 = 0
while (u || i < 2) {
    i += 1
    print(i)
}
print(99)
